Android STK in the unified game checkout
======================================
Android: SuperTuxKart, com.motorica.games.stk, SuperTuxKartActivity,
version 1.0.16 (1016). iOS: Fluxara Drift. Both use the common src/ engine.

Requirements: Java 17+, Android SDK 35 and NDK 26.3.11579264. Configure
sdk.dir in local.properties or set ANDROID_HOME. Keep the source-compatible
vendored libraries in ../lib, dependency slices in deps-armeabi-v7a and
deps-arm64-v8a, and the Mesa JNI libraries in mesa/.

Build from this directory:
    ./make.sh
    BUILD_TYPE=release ./make.sh

Both armeabi-v7a and arm64-v8a are included by default. COMPILE_ARCH can
select one ABI; CPU_CORE controls native build parallelism (default -j4).
Gradle automatically packages ResourceSource and AppResources and compiles
SDL Java code directly from ../lib/sdl2. Build outputs stay under build/.
No previous APK, downloaded catalog, or old STK checkout is required.

The application binds com.motorica.gamecontrol.BIND in com.bailout.stickk.
Its AIDL definitions match Motorica Start. Retain this package, Activity,
Binder interface and JNI class name when updating the common engine.

Release signing uses external Gradle properties:
    motoricaReleaseStoreFile
    motoricaReleaseStorePassword
    motoricaReleaseKeyAlias
    motoricaReleaseKeyPassword
Keep signing keys and passwords outside Git. The make.sh wrapper also
accepts the legacy STK_KEYSTORE, STK_STOREPASS and STK_ALIAS environment
variables. A standard debug build uses the Android debug certificate.

Generated data and build products can be removed with ./make.sh clean.
ResourceSource and AppResources are permanent source inputs. The optional
generate_assets.sh exports ResourceSource to OUTPUT_PATH for inspection;
normal builds do not need this export.
